%[text] %[text:anchor:T_81CFF743] # Implementing the Chaos Game
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../MainMenu.m)
%[text] Using the branching and looping controls from [Branches](file:Branches.m) and [Loops](file:Loops.m), this script will walk you through building out an implementation of the chaos game from bare bones to the ability to generate intricate designs automatically. 
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![A fractal with four-fold rotational symmetry](text:image:2b4c) ![Concentric circular colors that blend into the next](text:image:9ab1) ![A square-based fractal with four-fold rotational symmetry as well as horizontal and veritical reflection symmetries](text:image:270c)
%[text] This project will increase your familiarity with branches and loops in a context where their utility is key to observing the desired results.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51183E7B] **Before you get started:**
%[text] This live script is intended to be used with the code visible and output inline. On **View** tab of the MATLAB toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Output Inline**. Alternately, select **Output inline** using the icon ![live script code hidden icon](text:image:6cb8) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![Idea symbol](text:image:6a65) Interacting with this live script will build some familiarity with MATLAB, as concepts and commands are introduced together, but some familiarity with the Live Editor environment was introduced in [Introduction.m](file:Introduction.m). A brief summary of the tools, tips, and suggestions from each script is gathered in [Collected Pro Tips](file:CollectedProTips.m). This script will use content that you are not expected to understand yet, but you are encouraged to practice your reference skills and explore the documentation to continue learning beyond what is required to complete this project.
%[text] ![Warning symbol](text:image:2043)   For an optimal experience, follow the instructions and steps in the given sequence. Proceed to a new section only after completing the preceding one, including running all code blocks.
